ADDRESS: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan
==================================================
Midtown Manhattan is the central portion of the  [LINK: (New York City) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City]   [LINK: (borough) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boroughs_of_New_York_City]  of  [LINK: (Manhattan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan] , serving as the city's primary  [LINK: (central business district) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_business_district] . Midtown is home to some of the city's most prominent buildings, including the  [LINK: (Empire State Building) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empire_State_Building] , the  [LINK: (Chrysler Building) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chrysler_Building] , the  [LINK: (Hudson Yards Redevelopment Project) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hudson_Yards,_Manhattan] , the  [LINK: (headquarters of the United Nations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Headquarters_of_the_United_Nations] ,  [LINK: (Grand Central Terminal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Central_Terminal] , and  [LINK: (Rockefeller Center) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockefeller_Center] , as well as several prominent tourist destinations, including  [LINK: (Broadway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broadway_theatre] ,  [LINK: (Times Square) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Times_Square] , and  [LINK: (Koreatown) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koreatown,_Manhattan] .  [LINK: (Penn Station) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Penn_Station]  in Midtown Manhattan is the busiest transportation hub in the  [LINK: (Western Hemisphere) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Hemisphere] . [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-4]

Midtown Manhattan is the largest  [LINK: (central business district) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_business_district]  in the world and ranks among the world's most expensive locations for real estate;  [LINK: (Fifth Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fifth_Avenue]  in Midtown Manhattan has commanded the world's highest  [LINK: (retail) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retail]  rents and had been ranked as the most expensive shopping street in the world before falling to second in 2024. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-5]  [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-FifthAvenueMostExpensiveStreetOnEarth-6]  Midtown Manhattan is the country's largest commercial,  [LINK: (entertainment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entertainment_industry] , and media center, and is also a growing  [LINK: (financial) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_center]  and  [LINK: (fintech) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fintech]  center. [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-ManhattanFinancialCapitalWorld-7]

Many of New York City's  [LINK: (skyscrapers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skyscraper] , including its tallest hotels and  [LINK: (apartment towers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tower_block] , are located in Midtown Manhattan. The neighborhood hosts commuters and residents working in its offices, hotels, and retail establishments, tourists and students. Times Square, the brightly illuminated hub of the  [LINK: (Broadway Theater District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theater_District,_Manhattan] , [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-TransformingTimesSquare-8]  [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-9]  [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-10]  [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-Joshua_Pramis-11]  [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-12]  is a major center of the world's entertainment industry. [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-13]   [LINK: (Sixth Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sixth_Avenue]  also has the headquarters of three of the four major U.S.  [LINK: (television networks) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Television_network] .

Midtown is part of  [LINK: (Manhattan Community District 5) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Community_Board_5] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-NYCPlanning-2]  It is patrolled by the 14th and 18th precincts of the  [LINK: (New York City Police Department) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City_Police_Department] .


# LOCATION #

Geographically, the northern boundary of Midtown Manhattan is commonly defined to be  [LINK: (59th Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/59th_Street_(Manhattan)] ; its southern boundary is less clear, and variously taken to be  [LINK: (34th Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/34th_Street_(Manhattan)] ,  [LINK: (23rd Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/23rd_Street_(Manhattan)] , or even  [LINK: (14th Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/14th_Street_(Manhattan)] .[ [LINK: (according to whom?) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Manual_of_Style/Words_to_watch#Unsupported_attributions] ] Midtown spans the entire island of Manhattan along an east–west axis, bounded by the  [LINK: (East River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_River]  on its east and the  [LINK: (Hudson River) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hudson_River]  to its west.[ [LINK: (according to whom?) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Manual_of_Style/Words_to_watch#Unsupported_attributions] ]  [LINK: (The Encyclopedia of New York City) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Encyclopedia_of_New_York_City]  defines Midtown as extending from 34th Street to 59th Street and from 3rd Avenue to 8th Avenue. [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-enc-nyc-14]

In addition to its  [LINK: (central business district) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_business_district] , Midtown Manhattan encompasses many neighborhoods, including  [LINK: (Hell's Kitchen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell%27s_Kitchen,_Manhattan]  and  [LINK: (Chelsea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chelsea,_Manhattan]  on the West Side, and  [LINK: (Murray Hill) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murray_Hill,_Manhattan] ,  [LINK: (Kips Bay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kips_Bay] ,  [LINK: (Turtle Bay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turtle_Bay,_Manhattan] , and  [LINK: (Gramercy Park) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gramercy_Park]  on the East Side. It is sometimes broken into "Midtown East" and "Midtown West", or north and south as in the  [LINK: (New York City Police Department) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City_Police_Department] 's Midtown North and Midtown South precincts.

