Midtown is the original district in the United States to bear the name and included historical but now defunct neighborhoods such as the  [LINK: (Ladies' Mile) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ladies%27_Mile_Historic_District] , along  [LINK: (Fifth Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fifth_Avenue]  from 14th to 23rd Street; and the  [LINK: (Tenderloin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenderloin,_Manhattan] , from 23rd to 42nd Street and from Fifth Avenue to  [LINK: (Seventh Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seventh_Avenue_(Manhattan)] .

