Important streets and thoroughfares

[LINK: (Broadway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broadway_(Manhattan)]

[LINK: (34th Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/34th_Street_(Manhattan)]

[LINK: (42nd Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/42nd_Street_(Manhattan)]

The border of Midtown Manhattan is nebulous and further confused by the fact that the term "Midtown Manhattan" can be used to refer either to a district or a group of neighborhoods and districts in Manhattan:

The area between 14th and  [LINK: (86th Streets) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/86th_Street_(Manhattan)]  includes roughly the center of Manhattan; however, the term Midtown Manhattan can also apply to the area between 31st Street and 59th Streets, although there are still office buildings south of 31st Street.

[LINK: (Manhattan Community District 5) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Community_Board_5]  is located from 14th to 59th Streets, generally between Lexington Avenue and Eighth Avenue. Community District 5 is largely coterminous with Midtown but also includes the  [LINK: (Flatiron District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flatiron_District] ,  [LINK: (NoMad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NoMad,_Manhattan] ,  [LINK: (Union Square) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_Square,_Manhattan] , and parts of  [LINK: (Gramercy Park) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gramercy_Park]  and  [LINK: (Rose Hill) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_Hill,_Manhattan] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-NYCPlanning-2]

Midtown proper (within the boundaries of Manhattan Community District 5, and excluding overlapping neighborhoods) is located from 34th to 59th Streets between Third Avenue and Eighth Avenue. [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-enc-nyc-14]

The "Plaza District", a term used by Manhattan real estate professionals to denote the most expensive area of midtown from a commercial real estate perspective, lies between  [LINK: (42nd Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/42nd_Street_(Manhattan)]  and 59th Street, from  [LINK: (3rd Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Avenue]  to  [LINK: (7th Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seventh_Avenue_(Manhattan)] , about a square kilometer or half a square mile.

" [LINK: (Midtown South) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_South] " can refer to the part of Midtown between  [LINK: (23rd Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/23rd_Street_(Manhattan)]  and around 42nd Street (although its northern boundary is defined differently depending on the source).

"Midtown West" can refer to the area between 34th and 59th Streets, and between 5th and 12th Avenues.

"Midtown East" can refer to the area between 42nd and 59th Streets, and between 5th Avenue and the East River.

In 1982, the City of New York identified the "Manhattan Core" as the area that includes some of the city's most populous neighborhoods, major institutions, parks and transit hubs, and the city's primary Central Business District (CBD), defined as Manhattan below 60th Street. [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-15]  The "Manhattan Core" includes some areas slightly further north of 86th Street in Manhattan, as well as the area below 14th Street. However, this definition is problematic because it ignores the fact that Manhattan has not one but two zones that are job centers, which are separated by a wide swath of low-rise (by New York City standards) residential development: Midtown (which is in Midtown Manhattan) and the  [LINK: (Financial District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_District,_Manhattan]  (also known simply as "Downtown" because of its location in southern Manhattan). In other sources, these districts are referred to as separate central business districts. [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-16]

Midtown Manhattan viewed from  [LINK: (Weehawken, New Jersey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weehawken,_New_Jersey] , in September 2021, in the afternoon.

Midtown Manhattan viewed from  [LINK: (Weehawken, New Jersey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weehawken,_New_Jersey] , in September 2021, at sunset.

Midtown Manhattan viewed from  [LINK: (Weehawken, New Jersey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weehawken,_New_Jersey] , in September 2021, at night.


# ECONOMY #

Midtown Manhattan, along with  [LINK: (Lower Manhattan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_Manhattan] , is one of the world's leading financial centers.

Midtown Manhattan is the world's largest  [LINK: (central business district) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_business_district] , with 400 million square feet (37.2 million m2) of office space in 2018. [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-ManhattanOfficeSpace-17]  Midtown contains the headquarters of major companies, including  [LINK: (4Kids Entertainment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4Kids_Entertainment]  (formerly), [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-18]   [LINK: (Barnes & Noble) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barnes_%26_Noble] , [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-19]   [LINK: (Bloomberg L.P.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomberg_L.P.] , [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-20]   [LINK: (Ernst & Young) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernst_%26_Young] , [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-21]   [LINK: (Calvin Klein) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calvin_Klein] , [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-22]   [LINK: (Cantor Fitzgerald) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantor_Fitzgerald] , [LINK: ([23]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-23]   [LINK: (CBS Corporation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CBS_Corporation] , [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CBSCorporation-24]   [LINK: (Citigroup) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citigroup] , [LINK: ([25]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-25]   [LINK: (Colgate-Palmolive) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colgate-Palmolive] , [LINK: ([26]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-26]   [LINK: (Cushman & Wakefield) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cushman_%26_Wakefield] , [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-27]   [LINK: (DC Comics) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DC_Comics] , [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-28]   [LINK: (Deloitte) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deloitte] , [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-29]   [LINK: (Duane Reade) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duane_Reade] , [LINK: ([30]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-30]   [LINK: (Estée Lauder Companies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Est%C3%A9e_Lauder_Companies] , [LINK: ([31]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-31]   [LINK: (Foot Locker) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foot_Locker] , [LINK: ([32]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-32]   [LINK: (Frederator Studios) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederator_Studios] , [LINK: ([33]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-33]   [LINK: (JPMorgan Chase) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JPMorgan_Chase] , [LINK: ([34]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-34]   [LINK: (Hess Corporation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hess_Corporation] , [LINK: ([35]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-35]   [LINK: (Kroll Inc.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kroll_Inc.] , [LINK: ([36]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-36]   [LINK: (L-3 Communications) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L-3_Communications] , [LINK: ([37]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-37]   [LINK: (Marsh & McLennan Companies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh_%26_McLennan_Companies] , [LINK: ([38]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-38]   [LINK: (Marvel Entertainment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvel_Entertainment] , [LINK: ([39]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-39]   [LINK: (MetLife) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MetLife] , [LINK: ([40]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-40]   [LINK: (MidOcean Partners) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MidOcean_Partners] , [LINK: ([41]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-41]   [LINK: (Morgan Stanley) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan_Stanley] , [LINK: ([42]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-42]   [LINK: (Nasdaq, Inc.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nasdaq,_Inc.] , [LINK: ([43]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-43]   [LINK: (NBCUniversal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBCUniversal] , [LINK: ([44]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-44]   [LINK: (The New York Times Company) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times_Company] , [LINK: ([45]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-45]   [LINK: (NexCen Brands) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NexCen_Brands] , [LINK: ([46]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-home-46]   [LINK: (Paramount Global) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paramount_Global] , [LINK: ([47]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-47]   [LINK: (Pfizer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pfizer] , [LINK: ([48]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-48]   [LINK: (Polo Ralph Lauren) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polo_Ralph_Lauren] , [LINK: ([49]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-49]   [LINK: (Saks Incorporated) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saks_Incorporated]  ( [LINK: (Saks Fifth Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saks_Fifth_Avenue] ), [LINK: ([50]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-50]   [LINK: (The Sharper Image) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sharper_Image] , [LINK: ([51]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-51]   [LINK: (Simon & Schuster) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simon_%26_Schuster] , [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CBSCorporation-24]   [LINK: (Six Flags) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Six_Flags] , [LINK: ([52]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-52]   [LINK: (TBWA Worldwide) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TBWA_Worldwide] , [LINK: ([53]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-53]   [LINK: (Thomson Reuters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomson_Reuters] , [LINK: ([54]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-54]   [LINK: (Warner Bros. Discovery) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warner_Bros._Discovery] , [LINK: ([55]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-55]   [LINK: (Time Warner Cable) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_Warner_Cable] , [LINK: ([56]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-56]   [LINK: (The Travelers Companies) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Travelers_Companies] , and  [LINK: (Univision Communications) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Univision_Communications] . [LINK: ([57]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-57]  The  [LINK: (New York Institute of Finance) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Institute_of_Finance]  is located in Midtown Manhattan. [LINK: ([58]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-58]

[LINK: (Haier) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haier]  operates its United States offices in the  [LINK: (Haier Building) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haier_Building]  at 1356 Broadway, formerly the headquarters of the  [LINK: (Greenwich Savings Bank) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenwich_Savings_Bank] . Haier held the opening ceremony on March 4, 2002. [LINK: ([59]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-59]   [LINK: (Sumitomo Corporation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumitomo_Corporation]  operates its New York office, the headquarters of the corporation's United States operations, at 600 Third Avenue, 10016 in the  [LINK: (Murray Hill) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murray_Hill,_Manhattan]  neighborhood. [LINK: ([60]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-60]   [LINK: (El Al) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Al] 's North American headquarters are in Midtown. [LINK: ([61]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-61]  The  [LINK: (Air France) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_France]  USA regional headquarters are in  [LINK: (125 West 55th Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/125_West_55th_Street]  in Midtown Manhattan. [LINK: ([62]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-62]  [LINK: ([63]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-63]   [LINK: (Hachette Book Group USA) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hachette_Book_Group_USA]  has its headquarters in 237  [LINK: (Park Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park_Avenue] . [LINK: ([64]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-64]  In 1994  [LINK: (Alitalia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alitalia]  considered moving its USA headquarters from Midtown to  [LINK: (Lower Manhattan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_Manhattan] , but decided to keep the offices where they were at the last minute. [LINK: ([65]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-65]   [LINK: (Global Infrastructure Partners) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Infrastructure_Partners]  has an office in Midtown Manhattan. [LINK: ([66]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-66]

Midtown Manhattan is home to the  [LINK: (headquarters) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Headquarters]  of  [LINK: (Major League Baseball) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Major_League_Baseball] , [LINK: ([67]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-67]   [LINK: (Major League Soccer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Major_League_Soccer] , [LINK: ([68]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-68]  the  [LINK: (National Basketball Association) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Basketball_Association] , [LINK: ([69]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-NBA-69]  the  [LINK: (National Football League) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Football_League] , [LINK: ([70]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-70]  the  [LINK: (National Hockey League) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Hockey_League] , [LINK: ([71]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-71]  the  [LINK: (National Women's Soccer League) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Women%27s_Soccer_League] , [LINK: ([72]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-72]  and the  [LINK: (Women's National Basketball Association) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women%27s_National_Basketball_Association] . [LINK: ([69]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-NBA-69]

[LINK: (Silicon Alley) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silicon_Alley] , the common  [LINK: (metonym) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metonymy]  for New York City's  [LINK: (high tech) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_tech]  sector, is based in  [LINK: (Midtown South) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_South] , specifically the  [LINK: (Flatiron District) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flatiron_District] . Prominent Silicon Alley companies in Midtown include  [LINK: (AppNexus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AppNexus] ,  [LINK: (Blue Apron) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Apron] ,  [LINK: (Gilt) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilt_Groupe] ,  [LINK: (Betterment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betterment_(company)] ,  [LINK: (Oscar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oscar_Health] ,  [LINK: (SoFi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SoFi] ,  [LINK: (Rent the Runway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rent_the_Runway] ,  [LINK: (Warby Parker) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warby_Parker] , and  [LINK: (WeWork) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WeWork] . The technology sector has been expanding across Midtown Manhattan since 2010. [LINK: ([73]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-TechManhattan1-73]  The  [LINK: (biotechnology) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biotechnology]  sector is also growing in Midtown Manhattan based upon the city's strength in academic scientific  [LINK: (research) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Research]  and public and commercial financial support. By mid-2014, Accelerator, a biotech  [LINK: (investment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Investment]  firm, had raised more than US$30 million from  [LINK: (investors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Investor] , including  [LINK: (Eli Lilly and Company) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eli_Lilly_and_Company] ,  [LINK: (Pfizer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pfizer] , and  [LINK: (Johnson & Johnson) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnson_%26_Johnson] , for initial funding to create biotechnology startups at the Alexandria Center for Life Science, which encompasses more than 700,000 square feet (65,000 m2) on  [LINK: (East 29th Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/29th_Street_(Manhattan)]  and promotes collaboration among scientists and  [LINK: (entrepreneurs) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entrepreneur]  at the center and with nearby academic, medical, and research institutions.
The  [LINK: (New York City Economic Development Corporation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City_Economic_Development_Corporation] 's Early Stage Life Sciences Funding Initiative and  [LINK: (venture capital) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venture_capital]  partners, including  [LINK: (Celgene) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celgene] ,  [LINK: (General Electric) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Electric]  Ventures, and Eli Lilly, committed a minimum of US$100 million to help launch 15 to 20 ventures in  [LINK: (life sciences) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_sciences]  and biotechnology. [LINK: ([74]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-74]

Real estate is a major force in Midtown Manhattan's economy, and indeed the city's, as the total value of all New York City property was estimated at US$914.8 billion for the 2015  [LINK: (fiscal year) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiscal_year] . [LINK: ([75]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-NYC_real_estate-75]  Manhattan has perennially been home to some of the nation's, as well as one of the world's, most marketable real estate, including the  [LINK: (Time Warner Center) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_Warner_Center] , which had the highest-listed market value in the city in 2006 at US$1.1 billion, [LINK: ([76]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-76]  to be subsequently surpassed in October 2014 by the  [LINK: (Waldorf Astoria New York) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldorf_Astoria_New_York] , which became the most expensive hotel ever sold after being purchased by the Anbang Insurance Group, based in China, for US$1.95 billion. [LINK: ([77]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-Robert_Frank-77]  In the same year, six of the top ten most expensive zip codes in the United States by median housing price were located in Manhattan, underscoring the borough's dominant position in the real estate market. [LINK: ([78]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-78]  When 450 Park Avenue was sold on July 2, 2007, for US$510 million, about US$1,589 per square foot (US$17,104/m2), it broke the barely month-old record for an American office building of US$1,476 per square foot (US$15,887/m2) based on the sale of 660  [LINK: (Madison Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madison_Avenue] . [LINK: ([79]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-79]  In 2014, Manhattan was home to six of the top ten  [LINK: (zip codes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zip_code]  in the United States by median housing price. [LINK: ([80]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-80]  In 2019, the most expensive home sale ever in the United States achieved completion in Midtown Manhattan, at a selling price of US$238 million, for a 24,000 square feet (2,200 m2)  [LINK: (penthouse apartment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penthouse_apartment]  overlooking  [LINK: (Central Park) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Park]  at  [LINK: (220 Central Park South) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/220_Central_Park_South] . [LINK: ([81]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-81]

The  [LINK: (COVID-19 pandemic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic]  and  [LINK: (hybrid work) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Remote_work]  models have prompted consideration of commercial-to-residential conversion within the neighborhood's real estate sector. [LINK: ([82]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-82]  In August 2023, Mayor  [LINK: (Eric Adams) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Adams]  announced a program aimed at creating "a 24/7, live-work, mixed-use neighborhood" in Midtown South though the conversion of commercial and office space to residential, as part of an effort to create 20,000 new residences citywide in a decade. [LINK: ([83]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-83]  [LINK: ([84]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-84]

According to  [LINK: (The Broadway League) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Broadway_League] , shows on  [LINK: (Broadway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broadway_theatre]  sold approximately US$1.54 billion worth of tickets in both the 2022–2023 and 2023–2024 seasons. Both seasons featured theater attendance of approximately 12.3 million each. [LINK: ([85]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-BroadwayLeagueStatistics-85]

Companies that used to have their headquarters in Midtown Manhattan include  [LINK: (American Airlines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Airlines] , [LINK: ([86]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-86]  [LINK: ([87]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-87]   [LINK: (American Comics Group) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Comics_Group] , [LINK: ([88]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-88]   [LINK: (American Overseas Airlines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Overseas_Airlines] , [LINK: ([89]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-89]   [LINK: (Central Park Media) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Park_Media] , [LINK: ([90]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-90]  [LINK: ([91]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-91]   [LINK: (Eastern Air Lines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Air_Lines] , [LINK: ([92]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-92]   [LINK: (GoodTimes Entertainment) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GoodTimes_Entertainment] , [LINK: ([93]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-93]   [LINK: (LJN) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LJN] , [LINK: ([94]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-94]   [LINK: (NewKidCo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NewKidCo] , [LINK: ([95]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-95]   [LINK: (Pan American World Airways) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pan_American_World_Airways] , [LINK: ([96]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-Final_Pan_Am_Departure-96]  Philip Morris Companies (now  [LINK: (Altria Group) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altria_Group] ), [LINK: ([97]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-97]  [LINK: ([98]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-98]   [LINK: (Trans Caribbean Airways) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans_Caribbean_Airways] , [LINK: ([99]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-99]  and  [LINK: (Trans World Airlines) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans_World_Airlines] . [LINK: ([100]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-100]  [LINK: ([101]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-TBMap-101]  [LINK: ([102]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-102]  In 1997,  [LINK: (Aer Lingus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aer_Lingus]  announced that it was moving its North American headquarters from Midtown to  [LINK: (Melville, New York) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melville,_New_York] , in  [LINK: (Suffolk County) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suffolk_County,_New_York]  on  [LINK: (Long Island) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Island] . [LINK: ([103]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-103]


# DEMOGRAPHICS #

Based on data from the  [LINK: (2010 United States census) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010_United_States_census] , the population of Midtown Manhattan was 28,630, a change of 2,823 (9.9%) from the 25,807 counted in  [LINK: (2000) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000_United_States_census] . Covering an area of 692.81 acres (280.37 ha), the neighborhood had a population density of 41.3 inhabitants per acre (26,400/sq mi; 10,200/km2). [LINK: ([104]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-PLP5-104]  The racial makeup of the neighborhood was 64.1% (18,351)  [LINK: (White) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_(U.S._Census)] , 4.6% (1,310)  [LINK: (African American) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_American_(U.S._Census)] , 0.1% (34)  [LINK: (Native American) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Native_American_(U.S._Census)] , 20.8% (5,942)  [LINK: (Asian) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asian_(U.S._Census)] , 0% (8)  [LINK: (Pacific Islander) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_Islander_(U.S._Census)] , 0.3% (92) from  [LINK: (other races) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Race_(United_States_Census)] , and 2% (569) from two or more races.  [LINK: (Hispanic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hispanic_(U.S._Census)]  or  [LINK: (Latino) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latino_(U.S._Census)]  residents of any race were 8.1% (2,324) of the population. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-PLP3A-3]

The entirety of Community District 5, which comprises Midtown Manhattan, had 53,120 inhabitants as of  [LINK: (NYC Health) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City_Department_of_Health_and_Mental_Hygiene] 's 2018 Community Health Profile, with an average life expectancy of 84.8 years. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 2, 20  This is higher than the median life expectancy of 81.2 for all New York City neighborhoods. [LINK: ([106]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-:21-106] : 53  [LINK: ([107]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-107]  Most inhabitants are adults: a plurality (45%) are between the ages of 25 and 44, while 22% are between 45 and 64, and 13% are 65 or older. The ratio of youth and college-aged residents was lower, at 7% and 12% respectively. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 2

As of 2017, the median  [LINK: (household income) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Household_income]  in Community Districts 4 and 5 (including  [LINK: (Chelsea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chelsea,_Manhattan]  and  [LINK: (Hell's Kitchen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell%27s_Kitchen,_Manhattan] ) was $101,981, [LINK: ([108]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CB4_5PUMA-108]  though the median income in Midtown individually was $120,854. In 2018, an estimated 11% of Midtown Manhattan residents lived in poverty, compared to 14% in all of Manhattan and 20% in all of New York City. One in twenty residents (5%) were unemployed, compared to 7% in Manhattan and 9% in New York City. Rent burden, or the percentage of residents who have difficulty paying their rent, is 41% in Midtown Manhattan, compared to the boroughwide and citywide rates of 45% and 51% respectively. Based on this calculation, as of 2018 [LINK: ([update]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Midtown_Manhattan&action=edit] , Midtown Manhattan is considered to be high-income relative to the rest of the city and not  [LINK: (gentrifying) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gentrification] . [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105]


# POLICE AND CRIME #

Midtown Manhattan is patrolled by two precincts of the  [LINK: (NYPD) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City_Police_Department] . [LINK: ([109]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-109]  Midtown North is patrolled by the 18th Precinct, [LINK: ([a]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-precincts-110]  located at 306 West 54th Street, [LINK: ([110]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-NYPD_18th_Precinct-111]  while Midtown South is patrolled by the 14th Precinct, [LINK: ([a]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-precincts-110]  located at 357 West 35th Street. [LINK: ([112]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-NYPD_14th_Precinct-113]  The precincts ranked 69th safest out of 69 patrol areas for per-capita crime in 2010. The high per-capita crime rate can be attributed to the low population of the area, as well as the high number of crimes committed against tourists. [LINK: ([113]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-114]  As of 2018 [LINK: ([update]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Midtown_Manhattan&action=edit] , with a non-fatal assault rate of 25 per 100,000 people, Midtown Manhattan's rate of  [LINK: (violent crimes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violent_crime]  per capita is less than that of the city as a whole. The incarceration rate of 297 per 100,000 people is lower than that of the city as a whole. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 8

The 18th Precinct has a lower crime rate than it did in the 1990s, with crimes across all categories having decreased by 82.1% between 1990 and 2022. The precinct reported 1 murder, 22 rapes, 154 robberies, 185 felony assaults, 205 burglaries, 2,065 grand larcenies, and 116 grand larcenies auto in 2022. [LINK: ([114]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-115]  The 14th Precinct also has a lower crime rate than in the 1990s, with crimes across all categories having decreased by 81.2% between 1990 and 2022. The precinct reported 8 murders, 23 rapes, 653 robberies, 502 felony assaults, 660 burglaries, 2,375 grand larcenies, and 68 grand larcenies auto in 2022. [LINK: ([115]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-116]


# FIRE SAFETY #

The main part of midtown Manhattan, between 34th and 59th Streets from Lexington Avenue to Eighth Avenue, is served by five fire stations of the  [LINK: (New York City Fire Department) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City_Fire_Department]  (FDNY): [LINK: ([116]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-FDNY_locations-117]

Engine Company 1/Ladder Company 24 – 215 West 38th Street [LINK: ([117]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-118]

Engine Company 23 – 215 West 58th Street [LINK: ([118]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-119]

Engine Company 26 – 222 West 37th Street [LINK: ([119]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-120]

Engine Company 54/Ladder Company 4/Battalion 9 – 782 8th Avenue [LINK: ([120]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-121]

Engine Company 65 – 33 West 43rd Street [LINK: ([121]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-122]

The greater Midtown area between 14th Street and 59th Street contains seven additional fire stations. [LINK: ([116]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-FDNY_locations-117]


# HEALTH #

As of 2018 [LINK: ([update]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Midtown_Manhattan&action=edit] ,  [LINK: (preterm births) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preterm_birth]  and births to teenage mothers in Midtown Manhattan are lower than the city average. In Midtown Manhattan, there were 67 preterm births per 1,000 live births (compared to 87 per 1,000 citywide), and 4 births to teenage mothers per 1,000 live births (compared to 19.3 per 1,000 citywide). [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 11  Midtown Manhattan has a low population of residents who are  [LINK: (uninsured) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Health_insurance_coverage_in_the_United_States] . In 2018, this population of uninsured residents was estimated to be 11%, slightly less than the citywide rate of 12%. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 14

The concentration of  [LINK: (fine particulate matter) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Particulates] , the deadliest type of  [LINK: (air pollutant) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_pollution] , in Midtown Manhattan is 0.0113 milligrams per cubic metre (1.13×10−8 oz/ft3), more than the city average. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 9  Eleven percent of Midtown Manhattan residents are  [LINK: (smokers) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoking] , which is less than the city average of 14% of residents being smokers. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 13  In Midtown Manhattan, 10% of residents are  [LINK: (obese) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Obesity] , 5% are  [LINK: (diabetic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diabetes_mellitus] , and 18% have  [LINK: (high blood pressure) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypertension] —compared to the citywide averages of 24%, 11%, and 28% respectively. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 16  In addition, 9% of children are obese, compared to the citywide average of 20%. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 12

Ninety-one percent of residents eat some fruits and vegetables every day, which is higher than the city's average of 87%. In 2018, 86% of residents described their health as "good", "very good", or "excellent", more than the city's average of 78%. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 13  For every supermarket in Midtown Manhattan, there are 11  [LINK: (bodegas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convenience_store] . [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 10

The nearest major hospitals are  [LINK: (Mount Sinai West) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Sinai_West]  in  [LINK: (Hell's Kitchen) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell%27s_Kitchen,_Manhattan] ; the  [LINK: (Bellevue Hospital Center) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellevue_Hospital_Center]  and  [LINK: (NYU Langone Medical Center) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NYU_Langone_Medical_Center]  in  [LINK: (Kips Bay) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kips_Bay,_Manhattan] ; and  [LINK: (NewYork–Presbyterian Hospital) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NewYork%E2%80%93Presbyterian_Hospital]  on the  [LINK: (Upper East Side) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upper_East_Side] . [LINK: ([122]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-123]  [LINK: ([123]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-124]  In addition,  [LINK: (Beth Israel Medical Center) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beth_Israel_Medical_Center]  in  [LINK: (Stuyvesant Town) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuyvesant_Town]  operated until 2025. [LINK: ([124]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-125]


# POST OFFICES AND ZIP CODES #

Midtown Manhattan is located within six primary  [LINK: (ZIP Codes) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZIP_Code] . West of Fifth Avenue, Midtown is located in 10018 between 34th and 41st Streets, 10036 between 41st and 48th Streets, and 10019 between 48th and 59th Streets. East of Fifth Avenue, Midtown is located in 10016 between 34th and 40th Streets, 10017 between 40th and 49th Streets, and 10022 between 49th and 59th Streets. The area southwest of Fifth Avenue and 34th Street, sometimes considered to be in Midtown, is part of 10001. Other areas between 14th and 34th Streets are covered by ZIP Codes 10003, 10009, 10010, and 10011, though these are generally not considered to be part of Midtown proper. [LINK: ([125]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-zipmaps-126]  There are also thirty-three ZIP Codes assigned to individual buildings or building complexes. [LINK: ([127]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-128]

The  [LINK: (United States Postal Service) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Postal_Service]  operates six post offices in Midtown:

Appraisers Stores Station – 580 Fifth Avenue [LINK: ([128]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-129]

Bryant Station – 23 West 43rd Street [LINK: ([129]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-130]

Grand Central Station –  [LINK: (450 Lexington Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/450_Lexington_Avenue]  [LINK: ([130]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-131]

Midtown Station – 223 West 38th Street [LINK: ([131]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-132]

Murray Hill Station – 115 East 34th Street [LINK: ([132]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-133]

Rockefeller Center Station –  [LINK: (610 Fifth Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Maison_Francaise_(Rockefeller_Center)]  [LINK: ([133]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-134]

The  [LINK: (James A. Farley Station) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_A._Farley_Building] , the city's main post office, is located at 421 8th Avenue. [LINK: ([134]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-135]  The post office stopped 24-hour service in 2009 due to decreasing mail traffic. [LINK: ([135]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-136]


# EDUCATION #

Midtown Manhattan generally has a higher rate of college-educated residents than the rest of the city as of 2018 [LINK: ([update]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Midtown_Manhattan&action=edit] . A majority of residents age 25 and older (78%) have a college education or higher, while 6% have less than a high school education and 17% are high school graduates or have some college education. By contrast, 64% of Manhattan residents and 43% of city residents have a college education or higher. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 6  The percentage of Midtown Manhattan students excelling in math rose from 61% in 2000 to 80% in 2011 and reading achievement increased from 66% to 68% during the same time period. [LINK: ([136]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-:17-137]

Midtown Manhattan's rate of elementary school student absenteeism is lower than the rest of New York City. In Midtown Manhattan, 19% of elementary school students missed twenty or more days per  [LINK: (school year) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/School_year] , less than the citywide average of 20%. [LINK: ([106]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-:21-106] : 24 (PDF p. 55)  [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 6  Additionally, 92% of high school students in Midtown Manhattan graduate on time, more than the citywide average of 75%. [LINK: ([105]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-CHP2018-105] : 6

There are no public elementary or middle schools in Midtown. [LINK: ([137]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-Zillow-138]

The  [LINK: (New York City Department of Education) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City_Department_of_Education]  operates the following public high schools in Midtown, serving grades 9–12: [LINK: ([137]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-Zillow-138]

[LINK: (Jacqueline Kennedy-Onassis High School) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacqueline_Kennedy_Onassis_High_School_for_International_Careers]  [LINK: ([138]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-139]

Landmark High School [LINK: ([139]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-140]

Murray Hill Academy [LINK: ([140]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-141]

Repertory Company High School for Theatre Arts [LINK: ([141]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-142]

Satellite Academy High School [LINK: ([142]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-143]

Private schools include  [LINK: (The Beekman School) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beekman_School] ,  [LINK: (Rebecca School) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebecca_School] , and a number of private languages and music centers (e.g.  [LINK: (Berlitz) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berlitz_Corporation] , American Language Communication Center, New York Language Center, [LINK: ([143]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-144]  Swan Music School, and the  [LINK: (New York Youth Symphony) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Youth_Symphony] ). The  [LINK: (La Scuola d'Italia Guglielmo Marconi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Scuola_d%27Italia_Guglielmo_Marconi]  Italian international school moved to West Midtown in 2016. [LINK: ([144]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-ClarkeNewbldg-145]

The  [LINK: (New York Public Library) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Public_Library]  (NYPL) operates the  [LINK: (Stephen A. Schwarzman Building) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Public_Library_Main_Branch]  (also the Main Branch), a reference branch at 476 Fifth Avenue. The four-story building, constructed in 1911, is known worldwide for its architecture and has several million items in its collections. [LINK: ([145]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-146] 
There are also five circulating branches in Midtown: [LINK: ([146]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-NYPL_locations-147]  [LINK: ([147]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-148]

The  [LINK: (53rd Street branch) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/53rd_Street_Library]  is located at 18 West 53rd Street. The three-level branch opened in 2016, [LINK: ([148]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-149]  replacing the former Donnell Library Center that had been open from 1955 to 2008. [LINK: ([149]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-150]

The 58th Street branch is located at 127 East 58th Street. The branch opened in a  [LINK: (Carnegie library) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnegie_library]  building in 1907 and moved to its current two-story space in 1969. [LINK: ([150]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-151]

The Grand Central branch is located at 135 East 46th Street. The two-story library opened in 2008. [LINK: ([151]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-152]

The  [LINK: (Stavros Niarchos Foundation Library) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stavros_Niarchos_Foundation_Library]  (or Mid-Manhattan library) at 455 Fifth Avenue re-opened in its current form in 2021 after renovations. [LINK: ([152]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-153]  Diagonally opposite the Main Branch, it has occupied this site in various forms since 1970. [LINK: ([153]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-154]

The Terence Cardinal Cooke-Cathedral branch is located in the basement of 560 Lexington Avenue, adjacent to the  [LINK: (51st Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/51st_Street_(IRT_Lexington_Avenue_Line)]  subway station. It opened in 1887 and is the second-smallest branch of the NYPL system. [LINK: ([154]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-155]

Two campuses of the  [LINK: (City University of New York) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_University_of_New_York]  (CUNY)—the doctorate-granting  [LINK: (CUNY Graduate Center) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CUNY_Graduate_Center]  and the  [LINK: (Stella and Charles Guttman Community College) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stella_and_Charles_Guttman_Community_College] —are located in Midtown, while  [LINK: (Baruch College) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baruch_College] , also of the City University of New York, is located in Midtown South.  [LINK: (Mercy College) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercy_College_(New_York)]  is situated at  [LINK: (Herald Square) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herald_Square] .


# TRANSPORTATION #

[LINK: (Pennsylvania Station) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pennsylvania_Station_(New_York_City)]  and  [LINK: (Grand Central Terminal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Central_Terminal]  are the two major railroad stations located in Midtown Manhattan. Penn Station serves  [LINK: (Amtrak) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amtrak] ,  [LINK: (NJ Transit) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NJ_Transit_Rail_Operations] , and the  [LINK: (Long Island Rail Road) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Island_Rail_Road]  (LIRR), while Grand Central serves the  [LINK: (Metro-North Railroad) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metro-North_Railroad]  and also serves the LIRR at  [LINK: (Grand Central Madison) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Central_Madison] . [LINK: ([155]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-156]  Penn Station is considered to be the busiest  [LINK: (transportation hub) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transportation_hub]  in the  [LINK: (Western Hemisphere) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Hemisphere] , servicing around 650,000 people per day. [LINK: ([156]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-157]  [LINK: ([157]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-158]

The  [LINK: (Port Authority Bus Terminal) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Authority_Bus_Terminal] , located at Eighth Avenue and 41st Street at the western edge of Midtown, is the city's main  [LINK: (intercity bus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercity_bus]  terminal and the world's busiest bus station, serving 250,000 passengers on 7,000 buses each workday. The building opened in 1950 and had been designed to accommodate 60,000 daily passengers. A 2021 plan announced by the Port Authority would spend $10 billion to expand capacity and modernize the facility. [LINK: ([158]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-PABT2008-159]  [LINK: ([159]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-NYT2021-160]  [LINK: ([160]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-Record2021-161]

The  [LINK: (New York City Subway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City_Subway]  and  [LINK: (MTA Regional Bus Operations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTA_Regional_Bus_Operations]  each operate several routes that go through Midtown. Additionally, the  [LINK: (PATH) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PATH_(rail_system)]  train to New Jersey terminates at  [LINK: (33rd Street and Sixth Avenue) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/33rd_Street_station_(PATH)]  in Midtown. [LINK: ([161]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-162]  [LINK: ([162]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-163]

[LINK: (Traffic congestion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic_congestion]  is common, especially for crosstown traffic. In 2011, a new system of  [LINK: (traffic light) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Traffic_light]  control, known as "Midtown in Motion" was announced, with the aim of reducing traffic congestion. [LINK: ([163]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-164]  Approximately 750,000 vehicles enter Midtown Manhattan on a fall business day. [LINK: ([164]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-165]  According to the 2011 Traffic Data Report for New York State, 777,527 vehicles a day went through select toll facilities into Manhattan. [LINK: ([165]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-166]


# GOVERNMENT INFRASTRUCTURE #

The  [LINK: (New York Supreme Court, Appellate Division) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Supreme_Court,_Appellate_Division] , First Department, is located at the  [LINK: (Appellate Division Courthouse) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Appellate_Division_Courthouse_of_New_York_State]  at 25th Street and Madison Avenue was completed in 1900 by architect  [LINK: (James Brown Lord) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Brown_Lord] , who used a third of the construction budget to decorate the building with statues and murals. [LINK: ([166]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-167]  The  [LINK: (Puerto Rico Federal Affairs Administration) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puerto_Rico_Federal_Affairs_Administration]  operates its New York office on the 22nd floor at 135 West  [LINK: (50th Street) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/50th_Street_(Manhattan)] . [LINK: ([167]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-168]


# DIPLOMATIC MISSIONS #

Several countries, including  [LINK: (Algeria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_diplomatic_missions_of_Algeria] , [LINK: ([168]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-169]   [LINK: (Argentina) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Argentina] ,  [LINK: (The Bahamas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_the_Bahamas] , [LINK: ([169]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-170]   [LINK: (China) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_China] , [LINK: ([170]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-171]   [LINK: (Costa Rica) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Costa_Rica] , [LINK: ([171]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-172]   [LINK: (Germany) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Germany] , [LINK: ([172]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-173]   [LINK: (Ireland) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Ireland] , [LINK: ([173]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-174]   [LINK: (Israel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Israel] , [LINK: ([174]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-175]   [LINK: (Jamaica) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Jamaica] , [LINK: ([175]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-176]   [LINK: (Japan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Japan] , [LINK: ([176]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-177]   [LINK: (Luxembourg) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Luxembourg] , [LINK: ([177]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-178]   [LINK: (Mexico) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Mexico] , [LINK: ([178]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-179]   [LINK: (Morocco) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Morocco] , [LINK: ([179]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-180]   [LINK: (Saudi Arabia) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Saudi_Arabia] , [LINK: ([180]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-181]   [LINK: (Singapore) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Singapore] , [LINK: ([181]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-182]   [LINK: (South Africa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_South_Africa] , [LINK: ([182]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-183]   [LINK: (South Korea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_South_Korea] , [LINK: ([183]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-184]   [LINK: (Ukraine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_Ukraine] , [LINK: ([184]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-185]  and the  [LINK: (United Kingdom) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomatic_missions_of_the_United_Kingdom] , [LINK: ([185]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-186]  have permanent missions accredited to the United Nations, and consulates-general accredited to the United States, in Midtown Manhattan. In addition, the Taipei Economic and Cultural Office of the Republic of China ( [LINK: (Taiwan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan] ) is in Midtown Manhattan. [LINK: ([186]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midtown_Manhattan#cite_note-187]


